$ /usr/bin/python3 /workspace/training/motion_budget.py --camera imx708 --altitude 30 --target-size 30

camera         : Pi Camera Module 3 (IMX708)
altitude       : 30 m AGL
native GSD     : 0.886 cm/px
target         : 30 cm -> 33.9 px (resolvable at >=20 px, tiled)

MOTION BLUR  (budget 1 px = 0.89 cm on the ground)
 speed m/s    km/h   max exposure    i.e.
----------------------------------------------
         1     3.6        8.86 ms   1/113 s
         2     7.2        4.43 ms   1/226 s
         3    10.8        2.95 ms   1/339 s
         5    18.0        1.77 ms   1/564 s
         8    28.8        1.11 ms   1/903 s
        12    43.2        0.74 ms   1/1355 s
        15    54.0        0.59 ms   1/1693 s

  Shorter exposure needs more light or more gain. Gain adds noise, and
  noise costs detections. This is why survey flying happens in bright
  midday light, and why a slower pass genuinely buys image quality.

ROLLING SHUTTER  (readout ~33 ms full frame -- MEASURE, do not trust)
  Top and bottom of one frame are taken 33 ms apart.
 speed m/s    km/h   top-to-bottom skew   verdict
----------------------------------------------------
         1     3.6              3.7 px        ok
         2     7.2              7.4 px    SKEWED
         3    10.8             11.2 px    SKEWED
         5    18.0             18.6 px    SKEWED
         8    28.8             29.8 px    SKEWED
        12    43.2             44.7 px    SKEWED
        15    54.0             55.9 px    SKEWED

  Max ground speed for <=5 px skew: **1.3 m/s (4.8 km/h)**

  Across ONE 30 cm target (34 rows) the readout is
  only 0.43 ms, so at 5 m/s the target itself is distorted by
  0.24 px. **Rolling shutter does not break detection.**

  What it breaks is frame geometry: the footprint is a parallelogram, not
  a rectangle. That silently corrupts georeferencing, area measurement,
  stitching and photogrammetry -- and it looks perfectly sharp while doing
  it. Vibration turns the same effect into visible 'jello'.

  So: detection can fly fast. Mapping cannot. Decide per mission.
